0. Instructions for the model doing the work
Paste this section, plus the one task you want done, into the model.

0.1 Project facts
Multi-school SaaS for schools. Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict (noUncheckedIndexedAccess on), plain pg (no ORM), PostgreSQL 17 with forced row-level security, zod 4, vitest 5, plain CSS.
src/lib/*.ts holds all business logic and SQL. src/app/(app)/**/page.tsx are server-rendered pages. src/app/(app)/**/actions.ts are server actions that parse FormData, call a src/lib function, then revalidate or redirect. There is no public API.
Every database call goes through withTenant(schoolId, accountId, async (db) => ...) (or withAuth / withPlatform / withProvisioning) from src/lib/db.ts. Each call is one transaction with the school context set. Tenant tables carry school_id and a row-level-security policy of the form school_id = app_school_id() AND (app_mode() = 'tenant' OR app_provisioning()) (see the loop at the end of db/migrations/0024_homework.sql).
Permissions are data in src/lib/permissions.ts; check with can() / require_(). Parents are auth.account.kind === "parent".
Pure rules live in *-logic.ts files with no database access (pattern: src/lib/notebook-logic.ts, src/lib/homework-logic.ts).
Handler-level tests mock @/lib/session, next/headers, next/navigation.
0.2 Hard rules (stop and report to the founder instead of working around them)
Do not edit protected files: db/migrations/**, scripts/migrate.ts, src/lib/{db,auth,session,crypto,ratelimit,permissions,env,schools}.ts, src/lib/admissions-retention.ts, tests/global-setup.ts, .env*, .local/**, .claude/settings*.json, .claude/hooks/**. A hook refuses them. For a protected change, write the exact diff and a risk note in your report; the founder applies it.
No new migration or access-policy change without a written design note and the founder's approval in chat.
No deployment, hosting choice, paid service, scheduler or background worker. The design needs none.
Invented data only. Never read or print .env or .local/.
Do not change any number in PILOT_RULES, any formula, or any threshold unless the task says so. They are proposals awaiting the school's approval; a silent change invalidates the simulation.
Never produce a rank, leaderboard, "active/passive" label, or any figure for a real child. Missing evidence is a status, never zero. A missing component makes the combined figure "pending"; its weight is never shared out.
The calculation must never read counselling, home-visit, complaint, fee, practice-game or admissions tables.
No package installs. No destructive Git. Do not commit or push unless told to.
One test run at a time (all tests share one database). Run one test file at a time.
page.tsx files export only names Next.js allows. Shared files (src/app/globals.css, src/lib/permissions.ts, docs/MASTER_ROADMAP.md, package.json, migrations) are edited by one person at a time, never by two tasks in parallel.
