3. Phase 1 — Strengthen the calculation (all FREE, start now)
P1-1 Evidence trace ("why is this figure what it is")
Goal: every figure can be explained from the inputs behind it, as the blueprint requires.
Files: src/lib/development-calc.ts, tests/development-calc.test.ts.
Do: add an optional ref?: string to each observation, paper and activity in DevelopmentInput. Add to DevelopmentResult a trace object: for each quality, { direct: number | null, contexts: { context, observations, mean }[], support: { measure, share, rate, value }[], refs: string[] }; for each component, the parts and counts used (for academic: per-subject percentage and weight; for habits: the counts behind each measure; for growth: before, now and gain per area, and goal values). Rounded to one decimal for display, computed from exact values.
Do not: change any figure. All 29 existing tests must pass untouched.
Tests: for student s1, assert the trace of OA shows direct 75, the on-time share 0.10 with rate 0.95 and the readable share 0.15 with rate 1, and that recomputing from the trace gives 80.9. Assert a quality with status insufficient_evidence still has a trace listing what exists.
P1-2 Optional context weights
Goal: let the school load its own per-quality context percentages without a code change.
Files: as P1-1 (run after it).
Do: add contextWeights?: Record<string, Record<string, Num>> to RuleSet (quality code → context → weight). When a quality has weights, the direct figure is the weighted average of context means over the contexts that have observations; contexts without a listed weight get weight 0 only if at least one observed context has a weight, otherwise fall back to equal weights. checkRuleSet rejects negative weights and unknown quality codes. Default: absent (equal weights), so no existing figure changes.
Tests: equal weights reproduce today's figures; weights { class: 3, group: 1 } on a quality with class mean 100 and group mean 50 give 87.5; unknown code throws.
P1-3 Age bands
Goal: qualities not applicable to a class are handled by the rule set, not by each caller.
Files: as P1-1.
Do: add bands?: { name: string; classLevels: string[]; notApplicable: string[] }[] to RuleSet and export notApplicableFor(rules, classLevel): string[]. computeDevelopment gains an optional classLevel in the input; the result is the union of the band's list and input.notApplicable.qualities. checkRuleSet rejects a class level in two bands and unknown codes.
Tests: a band removing SD and ST gives qualitiesApplicable 13 and the 60% rule needs 8.
P1-4 Declared first-period option and tidy-up
Files: as P1-1.
Do: add firstPeriod: "pending" | "four_components" to RuleSet (pilot value "pending"). With "four_components" and input.previous === null, the combined figure is the weighted average of the other four components re-based to their own weights, and combined carries basis: "four_components" so the report can print it. With any other missing component it stays pending. Also: replace the odd rounding in growthGains with a round2 helper; remove the unused generic in rounded.
Tests: s8 with all of qualities and participation supplied and no previous period: pending under "pending", a figure with basis under "four_components"; s9 stays pending under both.
